    <h1>Transform With Science</h1>
    <p><strong>Privacy Policy (Terms & Conditions)</strong></p>
    <p class="updated-date">Last Updated: September 4, 2026</p>

    <p>This Privacy Policy explains how Transform with Science ("we," "us," "our," or the "App") collects, uses, stores, and protects information when you use our mobile application and related services.</p>
    <p>By using Transform with Science, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.</p>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We collect information that you provide directly to us when you use the App, as well as certain information that may be collected automatically.</p>

    <h3>1.1 Health, Body, and Nutrition Information</h3>
    <p>To provide the App's health and nutrition features, you may provide information such as:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Age, sex, height, and weight</li>
        <li>Body shape or body type</li>
        <li>Fitness or nutrition goals</li>
        <li>Daily calorie targets and macro-nutrient targets</li>
        <li>Food, diet, and meal entries with nutritional information</li>
        <li>Exercise or activity information, where applicable</li>
        <li>Other information you voluntarily enter into the App for calculating or tracking your health and nutrition goals</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This information is used primarily to provide features such as BMI calculations, estimated Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE), calorie recommendations, macro-nutrient calculations, and diet/nutrition tracking or any other related calculation within the App.</p>

    <h3>1.2 Account Information</h3>
    <p>If the App allows or requires you to create an account, we may collect information associated with your account, such as:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>Account identifier</li>
        <li>Login/authentication information</li>
        <li>Subscription or purchase status</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not require you to provide information that is not necessary for the functionality of the App.</p>

    <h3>1.3 Diet and Food Logs</h3>
    <p>When you use the App to record your diet, meals, or food consumption, we may collect and store the information you enter, such as food items, quantities, meals, calories, carbohydrates, proteins, fats, and other nutritional information. This information is used to provide your personal nutrition and macro-tracking features.</p>

    <h3>1.4 Device and Technical Information</h3>
    <p>We may automatically collect certain technical information when you use the App, including, where applicable:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Device type, model, and operating system version</li>
        <li>App version, language, and general region</li>
        <li>IP address and network information</li>
        <li>Mobile advertising identifiers and unique device identifiers</li>
        <li>Crash reports, diagnostic information, and general usage/interaction patterns</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>1.5 Information Collected Through Third-Party Services</h3>
    <p>We may use third-party service providers to support certain App functions, such as analytics, crash reporting, advertising, authentication, cloud storage, payment processing, or other technical services. These providers may collect or process information in accordance with their own privacy policies and applicable laws.</p>

    <h3>1.6 Health Platform Integrations (Apple HealthKit & Google Health Connect)</h3>
    <p>If you choose to sync Transform with Science with third-party health repositories such as Apple HealthKit or Google Health Connect condition to availability of this feature in App:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>We only read and write data that you explicitly grant permission for through your device permissions.</li>
        <li>Data obtained through Apple HealthKit or Google Health Connect is used solely to provide and improve the App's health tracking features.</li>
        <li>We do NOT use data collected from Apple HealthKit or Google Health Connect for marketing, advertising, or cross-app tracking purposes.</li>
        <li>We do NOT sell data derived from HealthKit or Health Connect to third parties, data brokers, or advertising platforms.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>We use the information we collect for purposes including:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Providing, maintaining, and personalizing Transform with Science</li>
        <li>Creating and managing your user account</li>
        <li>Calculating BMI, BMR, estimating TDEE, and providing calorie and macronutrient recommendations</li>
        <li>Allowing you to set, monitor, and manage food, diet, and nutrition logs</li>
        <li>Processing subscriptions, in-app purchases, and customer support inquiries</li>
        <li>Identifying technical issues, monitoring performance, and improving App stability</li>
        <li>Preventing fraud, abuse, and unauthorized activity</li>
        <li>Displaying non-personalized or personalized advertisements, where applicable</li>
        <li>Complying with legal obligations and enforcing our legal terms</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>IMPORTANT MEDICAL DISCLAIMER:</strong> We do not use your health or nutrition information to provide medical diagnosis or treatment. Transform with Science is intended for informational and educational purposes only and is not a substitute for professional medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment.</p>

    <h2>3. You Have Control Over Your Data</h2>
    <p>We want you to have full control over your Personal Data. You can manage, update, or delete your data directly through the App.</p>
    <p><strong>Delete Your Data:</strong> You have the right to request deletion of your Personal Data. You can delete your account and associated data directly from the App by navigating to <code>Profile > Security > Delete Account</code> and following the on-screen instructions. Note: When you delete your account, your profile and associated health logs will be permanently deleted and cannot be recovered.</p>
    <p><strong>Edit Your Data:</strong> You can review and update your profile information (age, sex, height, weight, body shape, goals) and modify or delete food and diet logs directly within the App.</p>
    <p><strong>Request a Copy of Your Data:</strong> Where applicable by law, you may request access to or an export copy of the Personal Data we hold about you by contacting us at the support details below.</p>

    <h2>4. How We Share Your Information</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your Personal Data for monetary payment. We may share limited information with third-party service providers when necessary to operate, maintain, and improve the App. Categories of service providers include:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Cloud Hosting & Data Storage (e.g., Supabase, Firebase)</li>
        <li>Analytics & Performance Monitoring (e.g., Google Analytics, Crashlytics)</li>
        <li>Authentication & Security Infrastructure</li>
        <li>Payment & Subscription Processing (e.g., Apple App Store/Google Play Billing)</li>
        <li>Customer Support & Ticketing Systems</li>
        <li>Advertising Networks & Attribution Partners</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>We retain your personal data for as long as your account remains active or as needed to provide you with App features. When you request account deletion through <code>Profile > Security > Delete Account</code>, your personal profile, health logs, and account identifiers will be permanently deleted or anonymized within 30 days, except where extended retention is required by law or fraud-prevention obligations. Encrypted system backups are fully overwritten within 60 days.</p>

    <h2>6. Data Security</h2>
    <p>We implement industry-standard technical and organizational security measures to protect your data from loss, unauthorized access, or disclosure. However, no internet transmission or electronic storage method is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

    <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>Transform with Science is not intended for use by children under the age of 13 (or 16 in the EU/UK). We do not knowingly collect personal data from children. If we become aware that a child has submitted personal data without parental consent, we will promptly delete it.</p>

    <h2>8. Your Regional Privacy Rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on your location (e.g., European Economic Area, UK, California, Canada), you may possess specific rights regarding your Personal Data, including rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, or port your data.</p>
    
    <h3>8.1 Notice for California Residents (CCPA / CPRA)</h3>
    <p>California residents have the following rights under the CCPA/CPRA:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Right to Know:</strong> Request categories and specific pieces of personal data collected over the past 12 months.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Delete:</strong> Request deletion of personal information held by us.</li>
        <li><strong>Do Not Sell or Share My Information:</strong> We do not sell data for money. However, sharing data with ad networks for targeted ads may constitute 'sharing' under CPRA. You may opt out via device tracking settings.</li>
        <li><strong>Non-Discrimination:</strong> We will not discriminate against you for exercising your privacy rights.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Third-Party Links</h2>
    <p>The App may contain links to third-party sites or services. We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of third parties.</p>

    <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy periodically. Changes will be reflected by the 'Last Updated' date at the top of this document. Material changes may be notified through an in-app popup or email alert.</p>

